      "message": "We actually provides backward compatibility support that returns RIL_RADIO_TECHNOLOGY_IWLAN when the device is on IWLAN in both AP-assisted mode and legacy mode. Here is the behavior in two different modes.\n\nAP-assisted mode:\nss.getNetworkRegistrationInfo(PS, WWAN).getAccessNetworkTechnology() \u003d LTE \nss.getNetworkRegistrationInfo(PS, WLAN).getAccessNetworkTechnology() \u003d IWLAN\n\nLegacy mode:\nss.getNetworkRegistrationInfo(PS, WWAN).getAccessNetworkTechnology() \u003d IWLAN \u003c-- unfortunately there is no way to know the actual cellular registration info in legacy mode.\nss.getNetworkRegistrationInfo(PS, WLAN).getAccessNetworkTechnology() \u003d IWLAN\n\nOr you can use mDefaultPhone.getTransportManager().isInLegacyMode() to distinguish between two modes.",
